            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="TRE01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Edward John</forename>
                        <surname>Trelawny</surname>
                        <addName>Trelwayney</addName>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1792-11-13">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1881-08-13"/>
                    <occupation>writer</occupation>
                    <occupation>adventurer</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>According to the <title>DNB</title>, Trelawny (1792-1881) sailed to America in Jan 1832 and returned in
    1835 which would discount a large number of these entries. But Mary Shelley notes in her diary
    that he sails for America in January 1833, which Godwin's entries would seem to confirm. It is not 
    clear to whom the 1806 entry refers (when Edward Trelawny would have been fourteen) and
    this has not been coded for Trelawny. </p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="other"><title>DNB</title>.</bibl>
                    <bibl type="printedbook"><title>The journals of Mary Shelley, 1814–1844</title>, ed. by Paula R. Feldman and 
    Diana Scott-Kilvert, 2 vols (Oxford and New York: Oxford University Press; Clarendon Press, 1987).</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
